<quiz><question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Calculating probabilities for a continuous Poisson random variable</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@num_elephants@} elephants are Poisson distributed in a park subdivided into {@num_regions@} regions of \( 1 km^2\) each, with no fences between them.</p>

<p>a. What is the probability that a given region contains {@num_close@} elephants? Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.</p>

<p>\(P({@num_close@} \text{ elephants} ) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>

<p>b. How many regions do you expect to have exactly one elephant? Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.</p>

<p>Expected regions \(=\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>

<p>c. How many regions do you expect to have no elephants? Give your answer correct to 2 decimal places.</p>

<p>Expected regions \(=\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text/>
    </generalfeedback>
